From: Ankit Pipalia <ankit@example.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 15:10:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] power: supply: qcom_smbx: override APSD high current

The driver programs 1.5 A for APSD DCP/CDP but immediately releases the
software ICL override for every source except the TCPM fallback.  On PM6150B
the programmed USBIN_CURRENT_LIMIT_CFG then remains 1.5 A while the effective
AICL status stays at the USB default 500 mA.  Under server load the charger
enters PAUSE_CHARGE and the battery discharges despite a capable input source.

Downstream smblib uses the high-current software override when setting a
numeric high-current ICL.  Do the same for the trusted APSD DCP and CDP cases,
while leaving SDP and the safe default under hardware/protocol control.  Keep
AICL and suspend-on-collapse enabled and rerun AICL only when entering or
raising an overridden request.

Signed-off-by: Ankit Pipalia <ankit@example.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c | 20 ++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
index 1..2 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
@@ -613,12 +613,16 @@ static int smb_apply_current_limit(struct smb_chip *chip, unsigned int current_ua,
 				   enum smb_icl_source source)
 {
-	bool fallback = source == SMB_ICL_TCPM_FALLBACK;
-	bool was_fallback = chip->icl_source == SMB_ICL_TCPM_FALLBACK;
-	bool rerun_aicl = fallback &&
-		(!was_fallback || current_ua > chip->requested_icl_ua);
+	bool override = source == SMB_ICL_TCPM_FALLBACK ||
+			source == SMB_ICL_APSD_CDP ||
+			source == SMB_ICL_APSD_DCP;
+	bool was_override = chip->icl_source == SMB_ICL_TCPM_FALLBACK ||
+			    chip->icl_source == SMB_ICL_APSD_CDP ||
+			    chip->icl_source == SMB_ICL_APSD_DCP;
+	bool rerun_aicl = override &&
+		(!was_override || current_ua > chip->requested_icl_ua);
 	int rc;
 
-	if (!fallback && was_fallback) {
+	if (!override && was_override) {
 		/* Downgrade: program safe limit while override still active, then release */
 		rc = smb_set_current_limit(chip, current_ua);
 		if (rc < 0)
@@ -629,7 +633,7 @@ static int smb_apply_current_limit(struct smb_chip *chip, unsigned int current_ua,
 			return rc;
 	} else {
-		/* Remove a previous software override before returning control to APSD. */
-		if (!fallback) {
+		/* SDP/default stay under the protocol-selected hardware ceiling. */
+		if (!override) {
 			rc = smb_set_icl_override(chip, false);
 			if (rc < 0)
 				return rc;
@@ -640,7 +644,7 @@ static int smb_apply_current_limit(struct smb_chip *chip, unsigned int current_ua,
 		if (rc < 0)
 			return rc;
 
-		if (fallback) {
+		if (override) {
 			rc = smb_set_icl_override(chip, true);
 			if (rc < 0)
 				return rc;
-- 
